CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
does not uniquely resolve
--
Regression for [class.conv.ctor] / [over.match.copy] in the
template-constructor fallback of
`user_defined_conversion_sequence`.

The trigger is a class with both an explicit single-arg ctor
and one or more template ctors (and therefore the
`has_template_constructor` flag).  Before the fix, an arg type
that the explicit ctor would accept (here `char[6]`) is admitted
as implicitly convertible to the class through the fallback
calling `new_temporary` (which uses direct-initialisation
semantics and accepts explicit ctors).  Reference-binding the
arg to `const T&` then succeeds, putting the implicit copy ctor
into the candidate set alongside the explicit `(std::string)`
ctor and triggering "does not uniquely resolve".
